  "card": {
    "title": "High-risk filter in PR list never flags large changes",
    "type": "feature",
    "scope": "# Summary\n\nThe \"high risk\" filter in the PR list never flags large changes — even PRs with thousands of lines changed are not marked high risk.\n\n# Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Open the PR list.\n2. Apply / view the high-risk filter.\n3. Observe a PR with a very large diff (thousands of lines changed).\n\nExpected: Large/high-impact PRs are flagged as high risk and surfaced by the high-risk filter.\nActual: No PRs get flagged as high risk, even ones with thousands of lines changed.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] PRs with large diffs (e.g. thousands of lines) are flagged as high risk\n- [ ] The high-risk filter surfaces those PRs\n- [ ] The risk score/field is populated and the size threshold is correct\n- [ ] Tests cover risk classification at boundary change sizes (just below / just above the threshold)\n\n# Dev Hints\n\n* Likely a broken risk-scoring calculation or filter predicate. Verify: is the risk field populated at all? Is the change-size threshold ever met? Is the filter comparing against the correct value?",
